 and insisting on being allowed to go up stairs , had entered the room in the abrupt manner which had so greatly alarmed his sister . In hopes of counteracting the fatal effects of the discovery which had unavoidably followed this interview , Godolphin was , on his return in the afternoon , introduced into the dining - room , which opened into Lady Adelina 's bed - chamber . The door was a - jar ; the partition thin ; and Mrs. Stafford was pretty well assured that the poor patient would be heard distinctly . Godolphin came in , pale from the conflict of his mind ; and all his features expressed anger and sorrow , with which he seemed vainly struggling . He bowed , and sat down in silence . Mrs. Stafford only was in the room ; and as soon as he was seated , said , in a low voice , yet with forced chearfulness — “
